  "_comment": "What scripts/check-upstream-releases.py watches: the specifications, TCKs and components no package manager covers (Dependabot reads npm, pip, Gradle, Dockerfiles and compose). `known` is the newest release this repo has taken into account; move it in the change that takes the next one in. `prerelease: true` also reports release candidates. `issue` is where the work for a new release goes. A `fork` block (eclipse-cfm/cfm) records the hub's fork: its base tag, the integration tag the images are built from, and each patch with what upstream would have to do for it to be dropped; on a new release the issue lists the routine of `fork.runbook`.",
